@crew torres-zeke
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== greet
? endgame:early
- {hi}! Still here. I keep checking. I told coil three, she'd been fretting.   #funny

== chat
? endgame
- Day nought, you held the rail on the ramp like it owed you money. Look at you now.   #funny
- No more lists to get on. Strange, isn't it? Good strange. Right, onward. To nothing much.   #warm
- So there's no next step. Fine. What would you learn just for fun? Properly, I mean.
? endgame:early
- Reyes left a note: "Coil three is glad." Coil three doesn't write notes. Reyes does.   #funny
? endgame beat:torres.6
- I've cast on another scarf. Shorter. Days-off colours. For you. Don't look.   #funny
? endgame:early beat:torres.4 tier>=friend
- Dad had a good day. He asked, "That new one of yours, did they stay?" I said yes, Dad.   #warm

== near
? endgame deck:6
- Hear that? She's settled. Ships know who's staying. Don't laugh. She does.

== feel
? endgame mood:high
- Sang to the coils all shift. They didn't complain. Neither did Calder. Two firsts.   #funny

== bye
? endgame
- Right, onward. Same time tomorrow. And the day after. I like saying that now.   #warm
